M013 changes behavior the spec determines. In `login`, the guard now uses `and`, so a registered user with a non-string password reaches `_hash` and raises instead of returning 401. The spec says `login` returns 401 for anything other than correct credentials, so I added tests for that.

M027 only changes the PBKDF2 iteration count. The hash is internal and never observable through the interface, so it is equivalent as far as the spec is concerned and I wrote no test for it.

