Both counterexamples report the `GatewayTimeout` exception escaping `pay`, and the spec requires 504 with nothing recorded. So the verifier is right and I fixed it.

My `except GatewayTimeout` only matched the exact class I had imported. If the gateway raised an exception of that name from another module or a subclass, it escaped instead of returning 504. `pay` now recognises a timeout by `isinstance` or by any class named `GatewayTimeout` in the exception's class hierarchy. Other exceptions are still re-raised. The pending attempt record keeps the amount and the gateway reference, so a retry with a different amount gets 409 and a retry with the same amount completes at most once. I also cleaned up the odd payment-id expression. I haven't run any of this.

